// `get_owning_side` then `get_controlling_side` (the neighbour's owner
// against OUR controller). Retail schedules exactly that way round -
// the neighbour's hypnotize ternary first at 0x43eaee, ours first at
// 0x43eb9c - so the two are not the same test written twice.
//
// AND THE ACCESSOR IS LOAD-BEARING, 1.09 of it. Spelling the owning
// side as the raw `combatSide` field the way is_enemy (0x442880) does
// leaves this body at 98.9103: on the SECOND condition VC6 folds the
// neighbour's side into the compare's memory operand AFTER the
// hypnotize ternary, where retail materialises it into a register
// BEFORE. Routing it through army.h's get_owning_side inline restores
// retail's order exactly - the same "an inlined accessor's value is
// materialised, not folded" barrier get_controller's own note records,
// now measured from the other side. The first condition is unmoved by
// it either way, because there nothing branchy stands between the
// operand and the compare.
